{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Fix f449 ADR citation for unbounded Jira DC reindex support\n\n## Problem\nThe f449 ticket description still cites \"ADR 0037 s3\" for the unbounded Jira DC reindex behavior, but ADR 0037 is now `oss-contribution-intake-posture`. The renumbered ADR that owns the **unbounded** Jira search-index-lag rule is `docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md` §3 (\"Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes\"). The Jira-family sub-seam context for DC search-index lag is also recorded in `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md`, in the \"Search-index lag\" row around line 282.\n\nThe current `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` module docstring already cites ADR 0055 rather than ADR 0037; this ticket will make that docstring citation explicit and consistent by naming `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` / the \"Search-index lag\" row, and by citing ADR 0085 §3 only for the unbounded-index-lag claim.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope for this ticket:\n- the f449 ticket description text (`f449-be6a-be56-4fef`, alias `seagreen-fortuitous-crayfish`);\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` module docstring only;\n- `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` only if the ADR wording itself needs consistency (expected read-only).\n\nOut of scope: other ADR 0037 references in live-harness/test documentation. A repo-wide grep will be reported so non-f449 stale references are visible, but this bug's fix is limited to the f449-era description/docstring citation.\n\n## Verification plan\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0037-oss-contribution-intake-posture.md` to confirm ADR 0037 is the GitHub PR / OSS contribution posture ADR, not Jira DC reindex support.\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md` §3 to confirm the unbounded search-index-lag statement.\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` around the \"Search-index lag\" row to confirm the Jira-family sub-seam citation target.\n- Run `grep -nE '\\bADR 0037\\b|0037 s3|oss-contribution-intake-posture|\\bADR 0055\\b|0055-jira-family-sub-seam|\\bADR 0085\\b' src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` and inspect the f449 description to prove the in-scope stale citation is gone and the replacement citation points to ADR 0055 / ADR 0085 according to each ADR's actual title and section content.\n- Run `grep -rnE '\\bADR 0037\\b|0037 s3' . | grep -iE 'reindex|Jira DC|Lucene|unbounded'` and record the hits, classifying each as in-scope (fixed here) or out-of-scope (reported).\n- Run the project verification commands (`make lint && make typecheck && make test`) after the docstring-only code change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The f449 ticket description no longer points readers to ADR 0037 / `oss-contribution-intake-posture` for Jira DC reindex behavior; it points the unbounded-index-lag claim to ADR 0085 §3 and the Jira-family search-index-lag context to ADR 0055 / `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` instead.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` cites `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` or ADR 0055 for the Jira-family sub-seam/search-index-lag support, cites ADR 0085 §3 only for the unbounded search-index-lag rule if it uses that claim, and contains no `ADR 0037` / `0037 s3` Jira-DC-reindex citation.\n- [ ] A repo-wide grep for `ADR 0037` / `0037 s3` near `reindex`, `Jira DC`, `Lucene`, or `unbounded` is recorded, with in-scope hits fixed here and any out-of-scope hits explicitly reported.\n- [ ] Project verification is green with the worktree virtualenv first on `PATH`.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788312857805086953,"uuid":"983a07d3-d0af-4854-8e45-9258bc6d6550"}